{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "כי שם ה' אקרא הצור תמים", :translit "ki shem hashem ekra hatzur tamim", :gloss "For the name of YHWH I call, the Rock, perfect"} {:he "ברוך דיין האמת", :translit "barukh dayan ha-emet", :gloss "Blessed is the true Judge"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Adjacent verses linked: Moses calling God's name 'the Rock' at his death parallels the blessing recited on hearing of death."}], :frame {:text "The blessing 'Blessed is the true Judge' (barukh dayan ha-emet) is the blessing mandated upon receiving news of a death, as codified in Berakhot 46b and Shulchan Arukh Orach Chayim 222:2. Moses recites this song, which constitutes his farewell, adjacent to his death.", :sources ["Berakhot 46b" "Shulchan Arukh Orach Chayim 222:2"]}} {:quotes [{:he "צדיק וישר הוא שחת", :translit "tzaddik v'yashar hu shachat", :gloss "Righteous and upright is He; He corrupted"} {:he "יפה דנתני", :translit "yafeh dantani", :gloss "He judged me well"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Reading 'shachat lo' — corrupted for Him — as prompting the acknowledgment 'He judged me well.'"}], :frame {:text "The obligation to accept divine judgment and declare 'He judged me well' (yafeh dantani) when suffering befalls a person is taught in Berakhot 60b, based on the requirement to bless God for the bad just as for the good.", :sources ["Berakhot 60b"]}} {:quotes [{:he "הוא עשך ויכוננך", :translit "hu as'cha veyechonan'cha", :gloss "He made you and established you"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Geographic adjacency of two verses reading 'He made you and established you' invites comparison."}], :frame {:text "The Ba'al HaTurim compares two adjacent occurrences of the phrase 'He made you and established you': one here in the Song of Ha'azinu, and one in Deuteronomy 32:6 in the preceding verse 'Is He not your father who acquired you; He made you and established you' (ha-lo hu avicha kanecha, hu as'cha veyechonan'cha), Deuteronomy 32:6.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 32:6"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Adjacent verses linked: Moses calling God's name 'the Rock' at his death parallels the blessing recited on hearing of death.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Reading 'shachat lo' — corrupted for Him — as prompting the acknowledgment 'He judged me well.'", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Geographic adjacency of two verses reading 'He made you and established you' invites comparison.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:40:51.798129175Z", :model "glm-5.2"}